@page "/help/inventory/purchase"

<PageTitle>Purchase Order Help - Vizar</PageTitle>

<div class="help-container">
	<!-- Header -->
	<div class="help-header">
		<div class="help-header-content">
			<button class="btn-back" @onclick='() => NavigationManager.NavigateTo("/inventory/purchase")'>
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<path d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7" />
				</svg>
				<span>Back to Purchase Order</span>
			</button>
			<h1 class="help-title">Purchase Order - User Guide</h1>
			<p class="help-subtitle">Complete guide to creating and managing purchase orders</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Content -->
	<div class="help-content">
		
		<!-- Overview Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
					<line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12" />
					<line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Overview</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>The Purchase Order page allows you to create, manage, and track purchase transactions from your suppliers. This comprehensive interface helps you maintain accurate inventory records, manage costs, and streamline your procurement process.</p>
				<p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
				<ul>
					<li>Multi-item purchase order creation</li>
					<li>Automatic tax calculations (CGST, SGST, IGST)</li>
					<li>Flexible discount management</li>
					<li>Real-time financial summaries</li>
					<li>Item identification tracking</li>
					<li>Auto-generated transaction numbers</li>
					<li>Data persistence across sessions</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Header Navigation Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2" />
					<line x1="9" y1="3" x2="9" y2="21" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Header Navigation</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>The header section provides quick access to navigation and important actions:</p>
				<div class="feature-grid">
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h4>🏢 Company Logo</h4>
						<p>Displays your company branding and identity.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h4>🗂️ Breadcrumb Navigation</h4>
						<p><strong>Inventory → Purchase Order</strong> - Click "Inventory" to return to the inventory dashboard.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h4>⬅️ Back Button</h4>
						<p>Returns to the main dashboard.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h4>🕒 History Button</h4>
						<p>Opens the transaction history to view past purchase orders.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h4>❓ Help Button</h4>
						<p>Opens this help guide (you're here!).</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Transaction Summary Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z" />
					<polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Transaction Summary</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>This section captures the essential details of your purchase transaction:</p>
				
				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Company <span class="required-indicator">*Required</span></h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Select the company branch or entity making the purchase.</p>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Click the dropdown and start typing to filter companies. If the company doesn't exist, you can create a new one by selecting the "Add New" option.</p>
					<p><strong>Note:</strong> This determines which company's inventory will be updated.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Party (Supplier) <span class="required-indicator">*Required</span></h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Select the supplier or vendor from whom you're purchasing.</p>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Type to search for existing suppliers. Select "Add New" to create a new supplier ledger if needed.</p>
					<p><strong>Note:</strong> The party selection may filter available items based on supplier relationships.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Transaction Date <span class="required-indicator">*Required</span></h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> The date when the purchase transaction occurred.</p>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Click the calendar icon to select a date or manually enter in DD/MM/YY format.</p>
					<p><strong>Note:</strong> This date determines the financial year and affects reporting periods.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Financial Year</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the financial year based on the transaction date.</p>
					<p><strong>How it works:</strong> Automatically calculated and shown in YYYY to YYYY format.</p>
					<p><strong>Note:</strong> This is read-only and ensures transactions are recorded in the correct fiscal period.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Transaction No</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Unique identifier for the purchase order.</p>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> You can manually enter a transaction number or check the "Auto Generate" checkbox to let the system create one automatically.</p>
					<p><strong>Auto Generate:</strong> When enabled, the field becomes read-only and a unique number is generated based on your company's numbering sequence.</p>
					<p><strong>Note:</strong> Transaction numbers help track and reference specific purchases.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Remarks / Narration</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Add notes, references, or additional information about the purchase.</p>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Enter any relevant details such as PO number, delivery terms, or special instructions.</p>
					<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use this field to maintain an audit trail and add context to the transaction.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Financial Summary Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23" />
					<path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Financial Summary</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>Real-time calculation of the total purchase amount including all charges and discounts:</p>

				<div class="calculation-flow">
					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>1. Base Total</h4>
						<p>Sum of (Quantity × Rate) for all items in the cart.</p>
						<p class="formula">Base Total = Σ (Item Qty × Item Rate)</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>2. Discount (-)</h4>
						<p>Total discount amount deducted from the base total.</p>
						<p class="formula">Discount = Σ (Item Discount Amounts)</p>
						<p class="note-text">Shown in red to indicate reduction.</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>3. After Discount</h4>
						<p>Base total minus discounts.</p>
						<p class="formula">After Discount = Base Total - Discount</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>4. Tax (+)</h4>
						<p>Total GST (CGST + SGST + IGST) on all items.</p>
						<p class="formula">Tax = Σ (CGST Amt + SGST Amt + IGST Amt)</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>5. After Tax</h4>
						<p>Total after adding taxes (or same as After Discount if tax inclusive).</p>
						<p class="formula">After Tax = After Discount + Tax (or After Discount if inclusive)</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>6. Other Charges</h4>
						<p>Additional charges like freight, handling, etc.</p>
						<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Enter a percentage, and the amount is calculated automatically.</p>
						<p class="formula">Other Charges Amt = After Tax × (Other Charges %/100)</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>7. Cash Discount</h4>
						<p>Additional discount offered for cash/early payment.</p>
						<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Enter a percentage to apply a further discount.</p>
						<p class="formula">Cash Discount Amt = (After Tax + Other Charges) × (Cash Discount %/100)</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step">
						<h4>8. Round Off</h4>
						<p>Adjustment to round the final amount.</p>
						<p><strong>Auto-calculated:</strong> System automatically rounds to the nearest whole number.</p>
						<p><strong>Manual override:</strong> You can enter a custom round-off value if needed.</p>
					</div>

					<div class="calc-step total-step">
						<h4>9. Total Amount</h4>
						<p>Final payable amount for the purchase order.</p>
						<p class="formula">Total = (After Tax + Other Charges - Cash Discount) + Round Off</p>
						<p class="note-text">Displayed prominently in blue highlighting.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="tip-box">
					<strong>💡 Tip:</strong> All financial calculations update automatically as you add items or modify values. Watch this summary to understand the final cost breakdown.
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Add to Cart Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<circle cx="9" cy="21" r="1" />
					<circle cx="20" cy="21" r="1" />
					<path d="M1 1h4l2.68 13.39a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.61h9.72a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.61L23 6H6" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Add Item to Cart</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>This section allows you to add items to your purchase order with detailed pricing and tax information:</p>

				<h3>Step-by-Step Process:</h3>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Step 1: Select Item <span class="required-indicator">*Required</span></h4>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong> Click the dropdown and start typing the item name or code. The system will filter matching items.</p>
					<p><strong>Auto-fill:</strong> When you select an item, the system automatically fills in:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Unit of Measurement (UOM)</li>
						<li>Current rate/price</li>
						<li>Default tax rates (CGST, SGST, IGST)</li>
					</ul>
					<p><strong>Add New Item:</strong> If the item doesn't exist, select "Add New" to create it.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Step 2: Enter Item Details</h4>
					<p>Fill in or modify the following fields in the first row:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Qty (Quantity):</strong> Number of units being purchased</li>
						<li><strong>Rate:</strong> Price per unit (auto-filled but can be modified)</li>
						<li><strong>Disc %:</strong> Discount percentage (0-100%)</li>
						<li><strong>CGST %:</strong> Central GST percentage</li>
						<li><strong>SGST %:</strong> State GST percentage</li>
						<li><strong>IGST %:</strong> Integrated GST percentage (for inter-state)</li>
						<li><strong>Remarks:</strong> Optional notes specific to this item</li>
						<li><strong>Tax Incl.:</strong> Check if the rate includes tax</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Step 3: Review Calculated Amounts</h4>
					<p>The second row displays automatically calculated values aligned with the input fields above:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Identification No.:</strong> Enter a unique identifier like serial number, batch number, or asset tag</li>
						<li><strong>Base Total:</strong> Qty × Rate (displayed below Rate field)</li>
						<li><strong>After Disc:</strong> Base Total after discount (below Qty field)</li>
						<li><strong>Disc Amt:</strong> Calculated discount amount (below Disc %)</li>
						<li><strong>CGST Amt:</strong> Calculated CGST amount (below CGST %)</li>
						<li><strong>SGST Amt:</strong> Calculated SGST amount (below SGST %)</li>
						<li><strong>IGST Amt:</strong> Calculated IGST amount (below IGST %)</li>
						<li><strong>Total:</strong> Final item total (below Remarks)</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="field-explanation">
					<h4>Step 4: Add to Cart</h4>
					<p><strong>Click the "Add" button</strong> to add the item to your cart.</p>
					<p><strong>Duplicate items:</strong> If you add the same item again, the quantities are combined.</p>
					<p><strong>Form reset:</strong> After adding, the form clears and focuses back on the Item field for quick entry of the next item.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="tip-box">
					<strong>💡 Tips:</strong>
					<ul>
						<li>All numeric fields update calculations in real-time as you type</li>
						<li>Use Tab key to quickly move between fields</li>
						<li>The "Tax Incl." checkbox affects whether tax is added to or included in the total</li>
						<li>Amounts in red indicate deductions (discounts)</li>
						<li>The Identification No. field is useful for tracking specific units, batches, or serial numbers</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Purchase Items Grid Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<path d="M3 3h7a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v14a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H3V3z" />
					<path d="M14 3h7v17h-7V3z" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Purchase Items Grid</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<p>The grid displays all items added to your purchase order cart with comprehensive details:</p>

				<h3>Grid Columns Explained:</h3>
				<div class="grid-columns">
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Item Name:</strong> Name of the purchased item
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Identification No.:</strong> Unique identifier (serial/batch number)
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>UOM:</strong> Unit of measurement (pcs, kg, liters, etc.)
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Qty:</strong> Quantity being purchased
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Rate:</strong> Price per unit
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Base Total:</strong> Qty × Rate
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Disc %:</strong> Discount percentage
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Disc Amt:</strong> Discount amount (shown in red)
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>After Disc:</strong> Amount after discount
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>CGST %, CGST Amt:</strong> Central GST details
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>SGST %, SGST Amt:</strong> State GST details
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>IGST %, IGST Amt:</strong> Integrated GST details
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Tax Total:</strong> Sum of all taxes
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Tax Incl.:</strong> ✓ if tax is included, – if tax is additional
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Total:</strong> Final line item total (shown in blue)
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Remarks:</strong> Item-specific notes
					</div>
					<div class="column-item">
						<strong>Actions:</strong> Edit and Delete buttons
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>Grid Features:</h3>
				<div class="feature-list">
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>🔍 Search</h4>
						<p>Use the search box at the top to quickly find items in the grid.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>🔄 Sorting</h4>
						<p>Click any column header to sort by that column (ascending/descending).</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>📊 Column Totals</h4>
						<p>The footer row shows aggregate totals for all numeric columns:</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Total Items count</li>
							<li>Sum of quantities</li>
							<li>Sum of all amounts</li>
							<li>Total discounts (in red)</li>
							<li>Grand total (in blue)</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>✏️ Edit Action</h4>
						<p>Click the blue edit icon to modify an item. This will:</p>
						<ol>
							<li>Remove the item from the grid</li>
							<li>Populate the "Add to Cart" form with the item's data</li>
							<li>Allow you to make changes and re-add it</li>
						</ol>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>🗑️ Delete Action</h4>
						<p>Click the red delete icon to remove an item from the cart immediately.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-item">
						<h4>🎨 Color Coding</h4>
						<ul>
							<li><span style="color: #dc2626;">Red numbers:</span> Discounts and deductions</li>
							<li><span style="color: #1e40af;">Blue numbers:</span> Totals and final amounts</li>
							<li>Alternating row colors for easier reading</li>
							<li>Hover effects highlight the current row</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="tip-box">
					<strong>💡 Pro Tip:</strong> The grid automatically updates all totals when you edit or delete items. Always review the footer totals before saving your transaction.
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Action Buttons Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2" />
					<line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="16" />
					<line x1="8" y1="12" x2="16" y2="12" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Action Buttons</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<div class="button-explanation">
					<h4>� Upload Document (Blue Button)</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Attach the original purchase invoice, bill, or receipt to the purchase order for record keeping.</p>
					<p><strong>What it does:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Opens a professional dialog for document management</li>
						<li>Allows uploading documents up to 50MB in size</li>
						<li>Stores documents securely in Azure Blob Storage</li>
						<li>Supports multiple file formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, PNG</li>
						<li>Provides download and remove functionality for uploaded documents</li>
					</ul>
					<p><strong>How to use:</strong></p>
					<ol>
						<li>Click the "Upload Document" button in the action buttons section</li>
						<li>In the dialog, either drag and drop your file or click "Browse" to select a file</li>
						<li>The file will automatically upload and be linked to the purchase order</li>
						<li>Once uploaded, you can download, interpret, or remove the document</li>
					</ol>
					<p><strong>Document Actions:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Download:</strong> Downloads the uploaded document to your device</li>
						<li><strong>Interpret:</strong> AI-powered document analysis (coming soon)</li>
						<li><strong>Remove:</strong> Deletes the document from storage and unlinks it from the order</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="note-text"><strong>Best Practice:</strong> Upload original invoices immediately to maintain accurate records and enable future auditing.</p>
					<p class="warning-text">⚠️ Maximum file size: 50MB. Supported formats: PDF, Word, Images (JPG, PNG).</p>
				</div>

				<div class="button-explanation">
					<h4>�💾 Save Transaction (Blue Button)</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Finalizes and saves the purchase order to the database.</p>
					<p><strong>What it does:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Validates all required fields</li>
						<li>Checks that at least one item is in the cart</li>
						<li>Verifies the financial year is open and not locked</li>
						<li>Saves the purchase order header and all line items</li>
						<li>Updates inventory quantities</li>
						<li>Updates supplier ledger balance</li>
						<li>Clears the cart after successful save</li>
					</ul>
					<p><strong>Required before saving:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>✓ Company selected</li>
						<li>✓ Party selected</li>
						<li>✓ Transaction date set</li>
						<li>✓ Transaction number entered (or auto-generated)</li>
						<li>✓ At least one item in cart</li>
						<li>✓ Total amount greater than zero</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="note-text">You'll see a success message when the transaction is saved, or an error message if validation fails.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="button-explanation">
					<h4>🗑️ Clear Cart (Gray Button)</h4>
					<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Removes all items from the current cart.</p>
					<p><strong>What it does:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Clears all items from the purchase items grid</li>
						<li>Resets the item entry form</li>
						<li>Resets financial summary calculations</li>
						<li>Does NOT clear transaction summary fields (Company, Party, Date, etc.)</li>
					</ul>
				<p><strong>When to use:</strong> If you want to start over with item selection but keep the transaction header details.</p>
				<p class="warning-text">⚠️ Warning: This action cannot be undone. All items will be removed from the cart.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Upload Document Section -->
	<section class="help-section">
		<div class="section-header-help">
			<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
				<path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4" />
				<polyline points="17 8 12 3 7 8" />
				<line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15" />
			</svg>
			<h2>Upload Document</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="help-text">
			<p>The Upload Document feature allows you to attach original purchase invoices, bills, or receipts directly to your purchase order. This ensures proper documentation and enables future reference and auditing.</p>

			<h3>Why Upload Documents?</h3>
			<div class="feature-grid">
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h4>📋 Record Keeping</h4>
					<p>Maintain complete purchase documentation in one place for easy retrieval and audit trails.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h4>🔍 Verification</h4>
					<p>Cross-reference entered data with original documents to ensure accuracy.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h4>📊 Compliance</h4>
					<p>Meet regulatory requirements for document retention and tax compliance.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h4>🤖 Future AI Analysis</h4>
					<p>Enable AI-powered document interpretation for automated data entry (coming soon).</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3>How to Upload Documents:</h3>
			<div class="workflow-steps">
				<div class="workflow-step">
					<div class="step-number">1</div>
					<div class="step-content">
						<h4>Access Upload Dialog</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Click the "Upload Document" button (blue button with upload icon)</li>
							<li>Located in the action buttons section below the transaction summary</li>
							<li>The professional upload dialog will open</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="workflow-step">
					<div class="step-number">2</div>
					<div class="step-content">
						<h4>Upload Your File</h4>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Drag & Drop:</strong> Simply drag your file into the upload area</li>
							<li><strong>Browse:</strong> Click the "Browse" button to select a file from your computer</li>
							<li>The file will automatically start uploading (no need to click upload button)</li>
							<li>You'll see a progress indicator during upload</li>
							<li>Success message appears when upload completes</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="workflow-step">
					<div class="step-number">3</div>
					<div class="step-content">
						<h4>Manage Uploaded Document</h4>
						<ul>
							<li><strong>Download:</strong> Click the blue "Download" button to save the document to your device</li>
							<li><strong>Interpret:</strong> Click the purple "Interpret" button for AI analysis (feature coming soon)</li>
							<li><strong>Remove:</strong> Click the red "Remove" button to delete the document and unlink it from the order</li>
							<li>Document information displays: filename and upload status</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3>Supported File Formats:</h3>
			<div class="field-explanation">
				<h4>✓ Accepted File Types</h4>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>PDF Documents:</strong> .pdf (Recommended for invoices)</li>
					<li><strong>Microsoft Word:</strong> .doc, .docx</li>
					<li><strong>Images:</strong> .jpg, .jpeg, .png (For scanned documents or photos)</li>
				</ul>
				<p><strong>Maximum File Size:</strong> 50 MB per document</p>
				<p class="note-text"><strong>Tip:</strong> PDF format is recommended for best compatibility and file size optimization.</p>
			</div>

			<h3>Document Security:</h3>
			<div class="feature-item">
				<h4>🔒 Secure Storage</h4>
				<ul>
					<li>All documents are stored in Azure Blob Storage with enterprise-grade security</li>
					<li>Files are encrypted during transmission and at rest</li>
					<li>Each file gets a unique identifier (GUID) to prevent naming conflicts</li>
					<li>Access is controlled through the application - no direct public access</li>
					<li>Documents are linked to specific purchase orders in the database</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<h3>Common Upload Scenarios:</h3>
			<div class="faq-item">
				<h4>📸 Uploading Photos from Mobile Device</h4>
				<p>If you're using a mobile device:</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Take a clear photo of the invoice using your device camera</li>
					<li>Click "Upload Document" button</li>
					<li>Click "Browse" and select "Camera" or "Photo Library"</li>
					<li>Select or capture the image</li>
					<li>The photo will upload automatically</li>
				</ol>
				<p class="note-text">Ensure the photo is clear, well-lit, and all text is readable.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h4>🖥️ Uploading Scanned Documents from Desktop</h4>
				<p>For scanned PDFs or documents:</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Scan the original invoice/receipt using your scanner</li>
					<li>Save as PDF (recommended) or image format</li>
					<li>Click "Upload Document" button in Vizar</li>
					<li>Drag the file into the upload area OR click "Browse" to select it</li>
					<li>Wait for upload confirmation</li>
				</ol>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-item">
				<h4>📧 Uploading Email Attachments</h4>
				<p>If you received the invoice via email:</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Download the attachment from your email to your device</li>
					<li>Open the Purchase Order page in Vizar</li>
					<li>Click "Upload Document"</li>
					<li>Select the downloaded file</li>
					<li>Upload completes automatically</li>
				</ol>
			</div>

			<h3>Replacing Documents:</h3>
			<div class="field-explanation">
				<h4>How to Replace an Uploaded Document</h4>
				<p>If you need to upload a different or corrected version:</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Open the Upload Document dialog</li>
					<li>Click the red "Remove" button to delete the current document</li>
					<li>Confirm the removal</li>
					<li>Upload the new document using the upload area</li>
				</ol>
				<p class="warning-text">⚠️ Note: Removing a document permanently deletes it from storage. This action cannot be undone.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="tip-box">
				<strong>💡 Best Practices for Document Upload:</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Upload documents immediately after creating the purchase order</li>
					<li>Use PDF format when possible for best quality and smallest file size</li>
					<li>Ensure scanned documents are clear and readable</li>
					<li>Use descriptive filenames before uploading (e.g., "Invoice_ABC123_2024.pdf")</li>
					<li>Verify the upload was successful before closing the dialog</li>
					<li>For large files, ensure you have a stable internet connection</li>
					<li>Keep original physical documents as per your company's retention policy</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="tip-box">
				<strong>⚡ Quick Tips:</strong>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Auto-Upload:</strong> Files automatically upload as soon as you select them - no upload button needed</li>
					<li><strong>Progress Bar:</strong> Watch the progress bar to see upload status</li>
					<li><strong>File List:</strong> Uploaded files show filename, size, and status</li>
					<li><strong>Download Anytime:</strong> You can download documents later for review or sharing</li>
					<li><strong>Mobile Friendly:</strong> Works seamlessly on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

