				<p>The system automatically saves your work to protect against data loss:</p>
				
				<div class="feature-item">
					<h4>💾 Automatic Saving</h4>
					<p>Your purchase order data is automatically saved to local storage whenever you:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Select or change the company</li>
						<li>Select or change the party</li>
						<li>Change the transaction date</li>
						<li>Toggle auto-generate transaction number</li>
						<li>Add an item to the cart</li>
						<li>Edit or remove cart items</li>
						<li>Modify other charges or cash discount</li>
						<li>Change round-off amount</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="feature-item">
					<h4>🔄 Data Recovery</h4>
					<p>If you close the page or your browser crashes, your data is preserved. When you return to the purchase order page, the system automatically:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Restores your unsaved transaction details</li>
						<li>Reloads all items in your cart</li>
						<li>Recalculates all financial summaries</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="feature-item">
					<h4>🧹 Data Cleanup</h4>
					<p>Local storage data is automatically cleared when you:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Successfully save a transaction</li>
						<li>Navigate away after saving</li>
					</ul>
					<p>This ensures you start fresh for the next purchase order.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="tip-box">
					<strong>💡 Best Practice:</strong> While auto-save protects your work, remember to click "Save Transaction" when you're done to permanently record the purchase order in the database.
				</div>
			</div>
