		<!-- Troubleshooting Section -->
		<section class="help-section">
			<div class="section-header-help">
				<svg class="section-icon-help" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
					<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
					<line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12" />
					<line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16" />
				</svg>
				<h2>Troubleshooting & FAQs</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="help-text">
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ Why can't I save my transaction?</h4>
					<p><strong>Possible reasons:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Company not selected</li>
						<li>Party (Supplier) not selected</li>
						<li>Transaction date not set</li>
						<li>Transaction number is empty (and auto-generate is off)</li>
						<li>Cart is empty (no items added)</li>
						<li>Financial year is locked</li>
						<li>Financial year is inactive</li>
						<li>Total amount is zero or negative</li>
					</ul>
					<p><strong>Solution:</strong> Check the error message displayed. It will tell you exactly what's missing or incorrect.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ Why are my tax calculations different from expected?</h4>
					<p><strong>Check:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Is the "Tax Incl." checkbox correct? If checked, tax is included in the rate, not added</li>
						<li>Are the CGST/SGST/IGST percentages correct for the item?</li>
						<li>Is the discount applied before tax calculation? (It should be)</li>
					</ul>
					<p><strong>Calculation Order:</strong> Base Total → Discount → After Discount → Tax → Total</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ Can I edit a saved transaction?</h4>
					<p>No, once saved, transactions are permanent for audit compliance. If you need to make changes:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Create a return/reversal transaction</li>
						<li>Create a new corrected transaction</li>
						<li>Contact your administrator if the transaction was saved in error</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ What happens to inventory when I save?</h4>
					<p>When you save a purchase order:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Inventory quantities are <strong>increased</strong> for all items</li>
						<li>Inventory is updated for the selected company only</li>
						<li>Item costs may be updated based on your accounting method</li>
						<li>The <strong>Net Rate</strong> is calculated for each item, which represents the true per-unit cost</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ How is the Net Rate calculated?</h4>
					<p>The Net Rate represents the actual per-unit cost of each item after applying all transaction-level adjustments:</p>
					<p class="formula">Net Rate = ((Total / Quantity) × (1 + Other Charges %)) × (1 - Cash Discount %)</p>
					<p><strong>Calculation steps:</strong></p>
					<ol>
						<li><strong>Per Unit Cost:</strong> Divide the item's total by quantity (includes base rate, item discount, and taxes)</li>
						<li><strong>Add Other Charges:</strong> Apply the Other Charges percentage from Financial Summary</li>
						<li><strong>Subtract Cash Discount:</strong> Apply the Cash Discount percentage from Financial Summary</li>
					</ol>
					<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
					<ul>
						<li>Item Total: ₹1,000 for 10 units = ₹100 per unit</li>
						<li>Other Charges: 5% → ₹100 × 1.05 = ₹105</li>
						<li>Cash Discount: 2% → ₹105 × 0.98 = ₹102.90</li>
						<li><strong>Net Rate = ₹102.90 per unit</strong></li>
					</ul>
					<p class="note-text">This Net Rate is stored with each purchase item and used for inventory valuation and cost analysis.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ What happens to the supplier ledger?</h4>
					<p>When you save:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>The supplier's (Party's) ledger is <strong>credited</strong> with the total amount</li>
						<li>This increases the amount you owe to the supplier</li>
						<li>The balance can be viewed in the supplier ledger report</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ Why did my items disappear after adding?</h4>
					<p>This is normal behavior. After clicking "Add," the item moves from the entry form to the grid below. Check the "Purchase Items" grid to see all added items.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ Can I use CGST+SGST and IGST together?</h4>
					<p>No. For each item, use either:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>CGST + SGST</strong> for intra-state purchases (within same state)</li>
						<li><strong>IGST</strong> for inter-state purchases (different states)</li>
					</ul>
					<p>The system allows both to be entered, but typically only one type should be used per item based on the supplier's location.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h4>❓ What is the Identification No. field for?</h4>
					<p>Use this optional field to track:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Serial numbers for individual units</li>
						<li>Batch numbers for production tracking</li>
						<li>Asset tags for fixed assets</li>
						<li>Lot numbers for quality control</li>
						<li>Any other unique identifier for specific inventory units</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="faq-item">
			<h4>❓ My document upload failed. What should I do?</h4>
			<p><strong>Common reasons and solutions:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>File too large:</strong> Maximum size is 50MB. Compress the file or split into smaller parts</li>
				<li><strong>Unsupported format:</strong> Use PDF, DOC, DOCX, JPG, JPEG, or PNG only</li>
				<li><strong>Network issue:</strong> Check your internet connection and try again</li>
				<li><strong>Browser cache:</strong> Clear browser cache and refresh the page</li>
				<li><strong>Timeout:</strong> For very large files on slow connections, try a smaller file size</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="note-text">If the problem persists, try converting the document to PDF and reducing the file size.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="faq-item">
			<h4>❓ Can I upload multiple documents to one purchase order?</h4>
			<p>Currently, each purchase order supports one document attachment. If you need to attach multiple documents:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Combine them into a single PDF using a PDF merger tool</li>
				<li>Upload the most important document (original invoice)</li>
				<li>Store additional documents in your company's document management system</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="note-text">Future updates may support multiple document attachments.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="faq-item">
			<h4>❓ What happens to the uploaded document when I save the transaction?</h4>
			<p>The document remains permanently linked to the purchase order:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>It's stored securely in Azure Blob Storage</li>
				<li>The document URL is saved in the database with the purchase record</li>
				<li>You can access it anytime from the transaction history</li>
				<li>The document persists even if you navigate away before saving the transaction</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<div class="faq-item">
			<h4>❓ Can I download documents on mobile devices?</h4>
			<p>Yes! The download functionality works across all platforms:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Downloads to your default downloads folder</li>
				<li><strong>Mobile (iOS/Android):</strong> Opens in native file viewer or saves to downloads</li>
				<li><strong>Web:</strong> Downloads through browser's download manager</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="note-text">On mobile devices, you may need to grant storage permissions.</p>
		</div>

